{"rule":"python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true","severity":"error","file":"bad.py","message":"Found 'subprocess' function 'call' with 'shell=True'. This is dangerous because this call will spawn the command using a shell process. Doing so propagates current shell settings and variables, which makes it much easier for a malicious actor to execute commands. Use 'shell=False' instead.","docs":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true","line":5,"col":32}
